{"term": "хуёк", "lang": "ru", "script": "cyrl", "romanization": "khuyok", "category": "organs", "subcategory": "penis", "concept": "penis", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_crude", "crude": 87, "technical": 3, "recognition_pct_current": 80, "recognition_pct_peak": 80, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Diminutive of хуй (the central Russian mat word for penis), meaning 'little cock'; used to imply smallness, with mock affection, or as a derogatory diminutive.", "english_term": "little cock", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Inherits full vulgarity of its root хуй despite the diminutive suffix -ок; the diminutive can function as endearing or contemptuous depending on context, a common feature of Russian diminutives applied to mat vocabulary."}
{"term": "причиндал", "lang": "ru", "script": "cyrl", "romanization": "prichindal", "category": "organs", "subcategory": "penis", "concept": "penis", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_neutral", "crude": 28, "technical": 5, "recognition_pct_current": 65, "recognition_pct_peak": 65, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Humorous colloquial term for the penis derived from a word meaning 'contraption' or 'thingamajig'; frequently appears in the plural (причиндалы) to mean male genitalia collectively.", "english_term": "contraption", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "The plural form причиндалы is more common than the singular and refers to the genitals broadly; avoids explicit vulgarity while remaining clearly sexual in context; the word's primary meaning is any mechanical gadget or doohickey."}
{"term": "агрегат", "lang": "ru", "script": "cyrl", "romanization": "agregat", "category": "organs", "subcategory": "penis", "concept": "penis", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_neutral", "crude": 33, "technical": 12, "recognition_pct_current": 60, "recognition_pct_peak": 60, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Literally 'unit,' 'aggregate,' or 'apparatus'; borrowed from mechanical and engineering vocabulary as a humorous colloquial euphemism for the penis, often implying impressive size.", "english_term": "apparatus", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Technical vocabulary repurposed for comic effect; the word choice implies scale and functionality; commonly used in boastful speech or jokes where the speaker wants to sound impressed by the anatomy in question."}
{"term": "удочка", "lang": "ru", "script": "cyrl", "romanization": "udochka", "category": "organs", "subcategory": "penis", "concept": "penis", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "euphemism", "crude": 15, "technical": 3, "recognition_pct_current": 52, "recognition_pct_peak": 52, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Literally 'little fishing rod'; a shape-based playful euphemism for the penis, used in mild humor and informal colloquial speech.", "english_term": "fishing rod", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Diminutive form conveys both small size and a softening of the crude reference; fishing imagery applied to male anatomy is cross-linguistically common; relatively infrequent compared to other Russian penis euphemisms."}
{"term": "пиписька", "lang": "ru", "script": "cyrl", "romanization": "pipis'ka", "category": "organs", "subcategory": "penis", "concept": "penis", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "euphemism", "crude": 7, "technical": 3, "recognition_pct_current": 95, "recognition_pct_peak": 95, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "The standard childish diminutive for the penis in Russian children's speech, derived from пи-пи (onomatopoeia for urination); also used humorously by adults.", "english_term": "pee-pee", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Despite being categorized under penis slang, пиписька can in children's speech refer to either sex's genitalia; it is one of the primary words Russian parents use when teaching young children about their bodies; adult humorous usage involves infantilizing register shift."}
{"term": "колышек", "lang": "ru", "script": "cyrl", "romanization": "kolyshek", "category": "organs", "subcategory": "penis", "concept": "penis", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_neutral", "crude": 22, "technical": 3, "recognition_pct_current": 48, "recognition_pct_peak": 48, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Literally 'little stake' or 'little peg'; a shape-based colloquial euphemism for the penis, suggesting a pointed or rigid object of modest size.", "english_term": "peg", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Less common than other penis euphemisms in Russian; the diminutive suffix implies small size, which can be humorous or mildly derogatory; primarily heard in informal storytelling and jokes rather than as a standard everyday slang term."}
