{"term": "малые половые губы", "lang": "ru", "script": "cyrl", "romanization": "malye polovye guby", "category": "organs", "subcategory": "vagina", "concept": "labia_minora", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "clinical", "crude": 3, "technical": 92, "recognition_pct_current": 75, "recognition_pct_peak": 75, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Literally 'small genital lips'; the standard clinical Russian term for the labia minora, the two inner folds of skin within the labia majora surrounding the vaginal opening.", "english_term": "labia minora", "english_translation_quality": "direct", "notes": "A direct calque of the Latin anatomical term; recognition is slightly lower than for большие половые губы, as awareness of the inner labia as a distinct anatomical structure is less consistently covered in basic health education."}
{"term": "пизда", "lang": "ru", "script": "cyrl", "romanization": "pizda", "category": "organs", "subcategory": "vagina", "concept": "vagina", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_crude", "crude": 98, "technical": 3, "recognition_pct_current": 99, "recognition_pct_peak": 99, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "The central Russian mat word for the vagina/vulva; equivalent in vulgarity to English 'cunt'; also used extensively as a general expletive, intensifier, and insult.", "english_term": "cunt", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "One of the canonical seven Russian mat words; its taboo level in formal and mixed-company settings arguably exceeds even English 'cunt'; nonetheless extremely common in informal male speech and increasingly in general colloquial usage; highly productive root (пиздёж, пиздатый, пиздануть, пиздец, etc.) making it perhaps the most morphologically generative Russian obscene word."}
{"term": "манда", "lang": "ru", "script": "cyrl", "romanization": "manda", "category": "organs", "subcategory": "vagina", "concept": "vagina", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_crude", "crude": 80, "technical": 3, "recognition_pct_current": 86, "recognition_pct_peak": 86, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "A crude vulgar slang term for the vagina/vulva; functionally synonymous with пизда but considered slightly less severe and somewhat more concentrated in Southern Russia, Ukraine, and parts of Central Asia.", "english_term": "cunt", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "More prevalent in Southern Russian dialects, Ukrainian Russian, and parts of Central Asia; less morphologically productive than пизда; used both as an organ name and as a general insult; etymology is uncertain, with possible connections to Romani or Turkic vocabulary."}
{"term": "киска", "lang": "ru", "script": "cyrl", "romanization": "kiska", "category": "organs", "subcategory": "vagina", "concept": "vagina", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_neutral", "crude": 28, "technical": 3, "recognition_pct_current": 92, "recognition_pct_peak": 92, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Literally 'kitty' or 'little cat'; a widespread mild euphemistic slang term for the vagina/vulva, equivalent to English 'pussy'; also common in pornographic and sexually playful contexts.", "english_term": "pussy", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "The cat-vagina double meaning parallels English 'pussy' and is similarly pervasive in Russian culture; mild enough to appear in mainstream comedy and popular media; widely used in pornographic contexts; the diminutive form adds a playful or affectionate tone."}
